---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import App from '../components/App.tsx';
import 'remixicon/fonts/remixicon.css';
import '../styles/index.css';
---

<Layout isApp={true} lang="en">
  <script is:inline src="/bezier.js" slot="head"></script>
  
  <App client:idle lang="en" slot="content" />

  <!-- Semantic HTML for Search Engine Crawlers & Screen Readers -->
  <section class="sr-only" aria-label="Tool Overview and Font Vectorization Guide">
    <h2>Google Font to SVG Path &amp; CAD DXF Converter</h2>
    <p>
      FontSVG is a free online tool to convert Google Fonts and custom fonts (.ttf, .otf, .woff, .woff2) into clean SVG paths (&lt;path d="..."&gt;) and CAD DXF drawings. 100% private in-browser parsing with OpenType.js and Maker.js.
    </p>
    <h3>Convert Google Fonts to SVG Paths Instantly</h3>
    <p>
      Search and render over 1,500+ Google Fonts directly in your browser. Generate clean, continuous vector SVG paths for web design, logos, icons, laser cutting, and CNC machining. Fully supports single Google Font queries as well as complete Google Fonts collections.
    </p>
    <h3>Upload Custom Fonts (TTF, OTF, WOFF, WOFF2)</h3>
    <p>
      Convert any desktop or web font file into SVG paths with zero server uploads. Full support for English typography, Latin scripts, and CJK characters (Japanese Kanji/Kana and Chinese Hanzi).
    </p>
    <h3>Boolean Union Welding for Cursive &amp; Script Outlines</h3>
    <p>
      Automatically merge overlapping script and cursive letter outlines using Maker.js boolean union. Prevents laser cutters, vinyl plotters, and Cricut machines from making unwanted overlapping cuts.
    </p>
    <h3>Export CAD DXF with Physical Units</h3>
    <p>
      Export industry-standard Autodesk DXF files formatted in millimeters (mm), centimeters (cm), or inches for CAD/CAM software including LightBurn, LaserCAD, Fusion 360, and Illustrator.
    </p>
    <h3>How to Convert Google Fonts to SVG Path &amp; CAD DXF</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Select a Google Font family or upload your custom .ttf / .otf / .woff font file.</li>
      <li>Type your text and customize font size, kerning, and line height.</li>
      <li>Enable 'Union' if converting cursive or script fonts with overlapping strokes.</li>
      <li>Click 'Copy SVG' to grab the raw &lt;path d="..."&gt; data or click 'Download SVG' / 'Download DXF'.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Layout>
